{
  "note": "A differential corpus for the probe redactor. Every entry is a synthetic diagnostic string, the pure form that was handed to libpq's own parse-only interface, and the credentials libpq recognised in that form. A recognised credential must not survive the redaction, and a form libpq recognises no credential in must come back unchanged.",
  "oracle": "PQconninfoParse (libpq 16.15 and 18.6), parse-only, no connection",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "conninfo: a plain password",
      "kind": "libpq",
      "text": "password=s3cret dbname=postgres",
      "libpq": "password=s3cret dbname=postgres",
      "libpqRejected": false,
      "libpqRecognisedCredentials": ["s3cret"],
      "secrets": ["s3cret"]
    },
